<title>UK: Great Western rail denies plans for 800 job cuts.</title>
<headline>Great Western rail denies plans for 800 job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Great Western Holdings, the new owners of the Regional Railways North West rail franchise, denied reports on Monday that it was planning to axe 800 jobs.</p>
<p>The denial responded to a statement put out by transport pressure group Save Our Railways (SOR), which said it had evidence that Great Western intended to cut 25 percent of the 3,200 workforce. It also claimed that MTL Ltd, the owners of Merseyrail in Liverpool, would cut 355 jobs, but MTL was not available for comment immediately.</p>
</text>
